493 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436247 1077 "selection" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436247 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436238 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436247 1079 #uuid "c1014636-1510-50f6-b488-e3fe8d24c13d" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436248 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436247 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436248 1069 "q-113603" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436248 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436248 1071 "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[x]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436248 1072 #uuid "0e4c9378-b054-5da6-b199-f46a138a46d3" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436248 1074 "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 4-6\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436249 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436246 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436249 1069 "q-113615" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436249 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436249 1071 "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $C$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436249 1072 #uuid "8d0458bf-0ded-5bc5-82a5-015d07a4533d" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436249 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the vectors of $C$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436250 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436251 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436250 1062 #uuid "4de2c56b-39c0-5e14-a7fb-e708db903e6f" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436250 1063 #edb/ref 17592186386696 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436251 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436252 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436251 1062 #uuid "4f40a8b0-4293-52f4-8c95-85c75998d506" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436251 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436248 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436252 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436254 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436252 1062 #uuid "77dfbfe9-ef7f-5713-be40-7bce1749b9a7" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436252 1063 #edb/ref 17592186247379 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436253 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436250 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436253 1062 #uuid "a2ad54ea-289c-5268-9e48-3009985055d0" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436253 1063 #edb/ref 17592186323807 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436254 1062 #uuid "f5e3b29d-0add-527d-a99b-25156b6317ea" 13194139534793 17592186045417 true] [17592186436254 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436249 13194139534793 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-3b5b7055-d6b7-5899-a741-daa60aef491a" 17592186436235 "answer-426822c2-147e-581d-8735-96a3bffe8321" 17592186436236 "answer-4ef4749a-0f85-5a2d-a5e3-df28976db7b9" 17592186436237 "answer-5c39bc95-ae02-5c17-9a57-15db094b94c3" 17592186436238 "answer-75556eec-